WEBVTT

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.980
Thank you very much, and good evening, ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:21.730
Here I am doing another TV show.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:25.320
And you know, this time, I really had a surprise for you.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.000
Matter of fact, this afternoon, I decided to get a crew haircut

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:42.290
and I finally got one and wouldn't you know I left it on the bus oh if any of

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:47.570
you are riding home on the bus tonight and you see a driver with a crew haircut

00:00:47.570 --> 00:01:00.000
you'll know it belongs to me you laugh I told the joke you laugh my writers are happy

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:04.510
But I'd like to have one thing cleared up once and for all.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:07.220
I do not wear a toupee.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:12.610
I mean, this is my own hair.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:14.480
When I say my own, I don't mean it's paid for.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:19.170
I mean, it's really droid.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:25.730
So, you know, I got a fan letter yesterday from a lady in--

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:29.150
I want to read this to you.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.550
This, uh...

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.930
Of course, I really don't need these glasses, you know.

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:39.210
I just wear them to keep my contact lenses from falling out.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:47.970
Of course, my contact lenses are pretty thick.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:51.140
In fact, the other day I left them in the kitchen,

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:55.110
and Rochester used one of them for a percolator cap.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:26.470
Well anyway, this letter is from a fan. It says, "Dear Mr. Benny, I've been a fan of yours for years and I can't tell you how much I've enjoyed your programs, but I've often wondered, after one of your shows is over, what do you do to relax? Please write and tell me. Yours very sincerely, it's funny I can't read the signature.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:59.860
Well, what she, uh, probably means is that, uh, you know, she knows that we work hard on a show and rehearsals, and what do we do for relaxation, naturally, after a show? So, well, we do one of many things. We might go to a movie, or go to a ball game, or go bowling.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:11.280
Well, let me take you back and show you exactly what I did after my last TV show.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:14.270
Now just, just stick around.

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:25.430
Sister, where's Mr. Benny?

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.700
He's still out there taking bows.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:28.760
Well, I have to go.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:30.000
Will you tell him how much?

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.720
- Have you enjoyed working on the show? - I certainly will.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.310
- Bye. - Bye.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:39.650
Boss is sure hiring young riders lately.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:45.780
I'm gonna put some of this stuff away.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:50.820
- Hello, boss. - Hello, Rochester.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:54.570
- Let me hang up your coat. - Thanks.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:57.130
You sent for a masseur like I asked you to?

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.000
- Yeah, he's on his way over. - Boy, I could show you.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:09.550
use a massage. You know, these television shows are hard work. Yeah, it's tough on both of us.

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:15.690
What do you mean, both of us? Boss, you only tell the jokes. I have to sit out there and laugh at them.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:23.900
That's the least you can do. Oh, Mr. Wilson. All right, Chester. Are you interrupting anything?

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:30.000
Now, come on in, Don. By the way, how did you like the show? I thought it was very good.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:33.000
- And Jack, your performance was excellent.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.020
- Well, thanks.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.340
How'd you like the orchestra?

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.160
