I'm just wondering, maybe,

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:50.960
you know how many times

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:52.380
we've wanted to get together?

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:54.930
And I've never...

00:19:54.930 --> 00:19:56.900
And so you see, if I didn't like it,

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:58.420
I don't know what I'm doing.

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:12.900
you know that i didn't mean to you know how i feel about you and gee well

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:30.000
i just never got the chance to tell you just how i felt you know as long as we're doing

00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:43.380
the chairs and tell you, you know how to meet me.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:13.410
Look at Gertrude, Gertrude, outside!

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:57.280
Now, Gertrude, as many times I've been coming here,

00:21:57.320 --> 00:21:59.120
this is the first time that's ever happened to me.

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:02.270
You made a spectacle of yourself.

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:07.110
I'm sure they will not mind. Come with me, please.

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:12.570
I regret to impose, but as you see, we are not prepared to accommodate such a large crowd,

00:22:12.570 --> 00:22:15.930
so if you do not mind, Mr. Pierrot would like to sit at your table.

00:22:15.930 --> 00:22:18.210
Well, look, we're so crowded.

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:20.820
Bonsoir, monsieur. Bonsoir.

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:24.940
Je compliment, monsieur. Il a un bien belle jeune fille.

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:27.260
What'd he say? What'd he say? What'd he say?

00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:30.000
He says you ought to be complimented on having such a beautiful

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:31.950
young companion.

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:33.670
Oh ho ho.

00:22:41.780 --> 00:22:42.660
What did he say then?

00:22:42.660 --> 00:22:47.540
He says, not only is she beautiful, but she has the fragrance of lilacs and roses.

00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:50.190
Wow.

00:22:50.190 --> 00:22:53.140
Il sent la grince de poulet.

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:54.140
What did he say?

00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:55.140
What did he say?

00:22:55.140 --> 00:22:57.430
He says, you smell like chicken fat.

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:11.340
I came here with my girl to have a nice quiet dinner all by ourselves.

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:14.400
And if we can't have any privacy, we're going home.

00:23:14.800 --> 00:23:16.220
Oh, but let me think.

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:17.680
Oh, but of course.

00:23:18.180 --> 00:23:19.560
The booth behind the curtain.

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:21.020
Come with me, please.

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:22.720
Now you're talking. Come on, girl.

00:23:32.910 --> 00:23:34.290
I will open the curtains for you.

00:23:37.070 --> 00:23:43.290
Hold the table in a minute.

00:23:46.420 --> 00:23:48.520
Michelle, get my green stamps.

00:23:48.620 --> 00:23:49.400
We're going home.

00:24:07.290 --> 00:24:08.390
Welcome to Mosley, Michelle.

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:11.590
Oh, Michelle, I'm so sorry about last night.

00:24:11.890 --> 00:24:13.610
Mr. Benny causing all that trouble

00:24:13.610 --> 00:24:15.990
and then leaving without paying his bill.

00:24:16.110 --> 00:24:17.770
Oh, don't worry about that.

00:24:17.850 --> 00:24:19.810
That has been taken care of.

00:24:19.920 --> 00:24:22.540
You have a dance, and I will find a table for you in a moment.

00:24:22.780 --> 00:24:23.680
Ah, merci.

00:24:23.680 --> 00:24:25.800
Merci.

00:24:40.200 --> 00:24:46.200
I am very sorry Monsieur Benny is busy at the moment, but he asked me to say goodnight for him.
